WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.567
-The January 6th hearings

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.367
have provided a mountain
of new evidence

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.467
about the relentless,
all-encompassing plan

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.367
by Donald Trump and his cronies
to overturn the 2020 election,

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.400
but maybe the biggest
revelation, so far,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.767
has been the degree to which the
people involved in the scheme

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.200
all had criminal intent

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.634
and knew what they were doing
was against the law.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:24.567
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:28.434
Look, I'm not especially hopeful
that the January 6th hearings

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.067
are going to magically
change the minds

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.267
of any hardcore Trump fans
in the Republican Party.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.167
I mean, I hope they do,
but we've been

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.501
through a seven-year-long
onslaught of Trump scandals,

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.167
including two impeachments;
a violent coup;

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.701
and a sex scandal,
in which he paid hush money,

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.934
during a presidential campaign,

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.801
to cover up an affair
with a porn star

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.934
and lied about it,

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.601
up until the point
where the actual check

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:55.033
he personally wrote
to make the payment surfaced

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.734
with his signature on it.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.200
And the way you know
that's Donald Trump signature is

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.801
that he looks like he signed it
with a giant Sharpie

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.367
while he was
white water rafting.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:08.267
Remember that whole thing?
Looking back now,

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.868
I have to say I always imagined
hush money

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.868
would be paid
in a more covert way

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.167
than writing
and signing a check.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:15.734
That was more like yell money.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.868
[ Laughter ]
I just assumed, from movies,

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.934
it would be an envelope full
of unmarked bills

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.968
passed between parked cars
down at the docks.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.567
I never would've imagined
Trump sitting down

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.701
to balance his checkbook,

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.801
going through all
the hush money payments.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:27.801
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] Alright, let's see.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.601
$150 for the cable bill.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.234
That's fair.
I watch a lot of cable.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.868
[ Laughter ]
$300 for groceries.

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.234
Eat a lot of groceries.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:37.601
Let's see, $130,000
to adult film star

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.400
to cover up sex scandal.
More than fair.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.000
[ Laughter ]
Mel!

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.367
Mel, honey, do you have
any hush money payments

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.567
you need me to make?

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.767
No, because I'm doing the bill

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.434
and, if you have hush money,
I'd love to --

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:52.000
Why? Because I don't want
to pay late fees.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.834
[ Laughter ]
Mel, I don't want to be

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:57.367
the only frugal one
in this relationship, Mel.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.501
None of that really seemed
to move the needle

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.567
with Republicans,
so I'm not optimistic

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:02.901
the January 6th hearings

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.767
are going to seriously
influence the GOP.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.701
But I am hopeful the hearings
will influence

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.467
prosecutors
in the Justice Department

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.934
because one area
where these hearings

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.634
have been shockingly successful

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.801
has been establishing
criminal intent

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.133
and a consciousness of guilt

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.400
among Trump and his gang
of pro-coup weirdos,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.167
as they were planning
and orchestrating the coup.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.601
Take disgraced former national
security advisor Michael Flynn,

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:27.067
who participated in discussions
where, among other things,

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.801
he pushed Trump
to use the military

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:29.834
to seize voting machines.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.734
Flynn invoked
the Fifth Amendment

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.167
during a series
of what you would think

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.000
would be pretty
straightforward questions,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.467
for any nonfascists.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.367
-Do you believe the violence
on January 6th

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:39.734
was justified morally?

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.033
[ Laughter ]
-You believe the violence

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.100
on January 6th
was justified legally?

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:53.434
General Flynn, do you believe

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.000
in the peaceful transition
of power

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.300
in the United States of America?

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:01.200
[ Laughter ]
You're pleading the Fifth

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.801
over a hypothetical that has
nothing to do with the law?

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.267
The Fifth Amendment
doesn't work like that.

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:06.501
It's not "Family Feud."

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:07.167
It doesn't say...

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.868
It protects you
from self-incrimination.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.667
And, look,
I'm generally very opposed

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.501
to drawing conclusions
about someone's guilt,

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:17.968
just because they
plead the Fifth.

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:20.634
It's a constitutional right
and it's in there for a reason.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.634
These are just
benign hypotheticals.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.434
This is like
if your spouse said,

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:25.801
"How do you feel
about monogamy?"

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.667
And your answer was,
"I'm invoking

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.367
my Fifth Amendment right not
to answer

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.901
any questions
about your sister."

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:35.367
It's not going to end
the conversation.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.901
That's how aware these guys were
that they were in legal trouble.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.200
They wouldn't even
answer questions

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.467
about whether they believe

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:41.801
in the peaceful transfer
of power.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.534
In fact, at almost every turn,
key White House officials

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:46.667
made it very clear
that they knew they were

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.968
in significant legal jeopardy.
For example, on Tuesday,

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.300
former Trump White House
official Cassidy Hutchinson

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.667
recounted, in a damning comment

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:56.167
from Trump's White House
counsel Pat Violoncello,

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.634
after he found out
that Trump wanted

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.634
to go to the Capitol himself
and lead the armed mob

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.267
in overthrowing
the election results.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.567
-We understand,
Ms. Hutchinson,

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.868
that you also spoke
to Mr. Cipollone

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.467
on the morning of the 6th,

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:10.934
as you were about to go
to the rally on the Ellipse,

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.300
and Mr. Cipollone said
something to you like,

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.567
"Make sure the movement
to the Capitol does not happen."

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:17.467
Is that correct?

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.734
-That's correct.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.200
I saw Mr. Cipollone
right before I walked out

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.300
onto West Exec that morning

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:28.067
and Mr. Cipollone said something
to the effect of,

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.734
"Please make sure we don't go
up to the Capitol, Cassidy.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.634
Keep in touch with me.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:35.434
We're going to get charged
with every crime imaginable,

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.601
if we make
that movement happen."

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.300
-And do you remember
which crimes

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.701
Mr. Cipollone
was concerned with?

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.501
-In the days leading
up to the 6th,

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:46.667
we had conversations

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.434
about potentially
obstructing justice

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:52.100
or defrauding
the electoral count.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.667
-It's amazing.
"We're going to get charged

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.434
with every crime imaginable."

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.634
It's truly mind-boggling to me

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:58.067
that none of these guys are
in jail, yet,

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.300
when they themselves were
expecting to end up in jail.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.701
Merrick Garland's still poring
over transcripts,

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:03.767
looking for a smoking gun.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.267
Meanwhile, on January 6th,

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.367
Trump aides were all
on Pinterest, searching for...

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:11.501
"Oh, cool!

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:14.367
It says you can bedazzle
your handcuffs!"

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.367
And, crucially,
that comment from Cipollone

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:19.067
was not just a one-time
freak-out on January 6th.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.267
As Hutchinson made clear
in that clip,

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.901
there were conversations
even before January 6th

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:25.801
about the likelihood that
Trump aides were committing,

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:28.100
among other crimes,
obstruction of justice

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.968
or defrauding
the electoral count.

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.701
Think about that.
They even named

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.667
the specific laws
they were breaking.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.667
They literally laid out
a blueprint

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.434
for prosecutors to arrest them.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:38.834
I mean, how much easier
can you make it?

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.968
This is like if, on every page,

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.234
Waldo was holding up
a giant sign that said...

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:48.501
That was not the only time
a White House lawyer

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.634
warned Trump cronies
that they were breaking the law.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.033
For example,
there was also Eric Herschmann,

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:54.334
whose job, it seems like,

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:56.534
was basically to tell everyone
in the Trump White House

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:58.067
they were constantly
breaking the law.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.667
Now, you might
remember Herschmann

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:01.200
from previous hearings,
as the guy

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.200
who has a baseball bat with the
word justice written on it

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.901
[ Laughter ]
hanging on his wall.

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:07.834
I like that it's not mounted
on wood

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.934
or in a glass case or anything.

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:12.667
It's just right there on hooks
at grabbing height.

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.100
[ Laughter ]
I bet, when people

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.667
got their lunches out of the
office fridge at his firm,

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.834
they triple-checked
they had the bag right.

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:20.701
[ Laughter ]
Herschmann was in a meeting

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.667
with another key figure
in the attempted coup --

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:24.667
Justice Department
official Jeffrey Clark.

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:27.968
Clark wanted Trump to make him
attorney general

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:30.834
after the election,
so that, as attorney general,

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:32.968
Clark could declare,
without evidence,

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:34.801
that there was fraud
in the election

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:36.367
and then overturn the results.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:39.300
And Herschmann had very blunt
words for Clark

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.334
when he found out
about Clark's plan.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:44.334
-When he finished discussing
what he planned on doing,

00:06:44.334 --> 00:06:46.934
I said, "Good [bleep]."

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:49.400
Excuse me. Sorry.
"Effing a-hole,

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.367
congratulations,
you just admitted the first step

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.167
or act you'd take
as attorney general

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.567
would be committing a felony."

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.234
-I like that the guy
has enough decorum

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.667
not to curse in a deposition,

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:59.634
but still keeps a baseball bat
in the frame,

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:02.868
[ Laughter ]
just to keep everyone on edge.

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:04.767
I wish I could've been
a fly on the wall

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:07.067
for all his conversations
in the White House.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:09.167
[ As Herschmann ]
If you break the law, I'm going
to use this baseball bat

00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:10.734
and beat the living [bleep]
out of you.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:12.834
Sorry!
The living eff out of you.

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.300
[ Laughter ]
Please,

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.968
please excuse
my horrible manners,

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:19.100
you dumb [bleep] piece
of [bleep].

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:22.901
So, yet again, we have
a Trump White House official

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.334
making it plain as day that
the people planning the coup

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:28.067
knew they were breaking the law
when they were doing it.

00:07:28.067 --> 00:07:30.434
For example, we also know,
from testimony given

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:33.100
by a former aide to Mike Pence,
that John Eastman,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.968
the pro-coup lawyer
who wrote the memo

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:37.501
detailing how Pence was supposed
to overturn the results

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:40.667
on January 6th,
also knew his plan was illegal.

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:43.234
Eastman admitted, in the
Oval Office, in front of Trump,

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:46.067
that his plan would violate
the Electoral Count Act

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:47.501
and, after the whole thing
descended

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.501
into violence and chaos
on the 6th,

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:51.367
Herschmann --
the baseball bat guy --

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:54.367
[ Laughter ]
again offered a very stark
warning to Eastman.

00:08:38.634 --> 00:08:39.400
I screamed...

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.234
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:47.234 --> 00:08:48.634
-And I screamed --

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:52.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.734 --> 00:09:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:05.801
[ Laughter ]
-Man, where did this guy
get his law degree?

00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:08.133
Does Yale Law School have
a building on campus called...

00:09:10.267 --> 00:09:11.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.868 --> 00:09:13.701
The only problem with that
library -- it's great,

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:15.067
but as soon as you learn
something there,

00:09:15.067 --> 00:09:16.834
you fuhgeddaboudit.

00:09:16.834 --> 00:09:19.601
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.467 --> 00:09:23.734
And, as we've also discovered,
from these hearings,

00:09:23.734 --> 00:09:26.901
Trump's cronies had such
a clear consciousness of guilt

00:09:26.901 --> 00:09:29.501
that a lot of them were asking
for preemptive pardons.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.667
They knew they could be
prosecuted and they wanted Trump

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:33.501
to get them off the hook
before that happened.

00:09:45.701 --> 00:09:47.968
-Dr. Eastman emailed
Rudy Giuliani

00:09:47.968 --> 00:09:50.234
and requested that he be
included on a list

00:09:50.234 --> 00:09:53.100
of potential recipients
of a presidential pardon.

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:12.734
-Did Rudy Giuliani ever suggest
that he was interested

00:10:12.734 --> 00:10:16.701
in receiving a presidential
pardon related to January 6th?

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.167
-He did.

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:22.234
-Ms. Hutchison, did White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:10:22.234 --> 00:10:24.033
ever indicate
that he was interested

00:10:24.033 --> 00:10:28.167
in receiving a presidential
pardon related to January 6th?

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.601
-Mr. Meadows did seek
that pardon, yes, ma'am.

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.934
[ Laughter ]
-At this point,
it's easier to ask

00:10:40.934 --> 00:10:42.901
who wasn't looking for a pardon.

00:10:42.901 --> 00:10:44.467
[ Laughter ]
Mr. President, here's a list

00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:46.267
of the people
who want pardons...

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:52.367
[ Laughter ]
and that kid who mow the lawn.

00:10:52.367 --> 00:10:53.667
Do you remember him?

00:10:53.667 --> 00:10:55.334
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, he needs a pardon.

00:10:55.334 --> 00:10:57.133
I guess he maybe stole
that lawnmower.

00:10:57.133 --> 00:10:58.968
[ Laughter ]
I just love the fact

00:10:58.968 --> 00:11:00.501
that Matt Gaetz was just
going around,

00:11:00.501 --> 00:11:02.000
telling people he asked
for a pardon,

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.667
like it was cool
and not incriminating.

00:11:03.667 --> 00:11:06.467
Although, Gaetz does seem
like a guy who doesn't know

00:11:06.467 --> 00:11:08.234
what he says makes him look bad.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:10.234
[ As Gaetz ]
Hey, Jeff was saying cold water

00:11:10.234 --> 00:11:13.234
makes his ween look small,
but I was like, "Dude,

00:11:13.234 --> 00:11:16.267
mine looks small, no matter
what temperature the water is.

00:11:16.267 --> 00:11:17.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
Am I right? Am I right?

00:11:17.801 --> 00:11:19.067
Herschmann, am I right?"

00:11:19.067 --> 00:11:20.667
[ As Herschmann ]
Shut the [bleep] up.

00:11:20.667 --> 00:11:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:11:21.501 --> 00:11:22.901
Shut the eff up.

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:24.901
[ Laughter ]

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:26.968
These hearings have sent
a clear message

00:11:26.968 --> 00:11:28.801
